        "from": "Savannah Boele <s.boele@essb.eur.nl>",
        "to": "\"amin@mail.avicennaresearch.com\" <amin@mail.avicennaresearch.com>",
        "cc": "Rick van Logchem <vanlogchem@essb.eur.nl>",
        "subject": "Avicenna ID's and phone numbers participants?",
        "reply_to": null,
        "message_id": "<PA4PR02MB7118088BF3C11E49F58781B1A1472@PA4PR02MB7118.eurprd02.prod.outlook.com>",
        "message_id_md5": "1757ede1808b654e3c99ffe45bd018a9",
        "in_reply_to": null,
        "content_type": "text/html",
        "body": "<div>\n<p>Hi Amin,</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Next Monday, we will begin the ESM and daily diaries for our four studies (4044, 4045, 4050, 4051). We have already requested participants to share their Avicenna ID with is, so that we can link their personal information, specifically their registered phone number, to their anonymous Avicenna ID. This is necessary to send personalized messages regarding their compliance through WhatsApp during the studies. However, to date, we still do not have each participant's ID. As we are close to starting, we were wondering whether there might be another way to gather their phone numbers.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>We are unable to locate this information through the researcher's dashboard. We can only see the list of Avicenna IDs. Is there a way to determine which phone number corresponds to each ID?</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Any assistance you can provide would be much appreciated.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Kind regards,</p>\n<p>Savannah and Rick</p>\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"width:356.25pt;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width:356.25pt;padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt;\">\n<div>\n<p><b><span style=\"color:#002328;\">Dr. Savannah Boele</span></b><span style=\"color:#002328;\"><br>\n</span><b><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:#ff9900;background:white;\">Postdoctoral researcher | Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences</span></b></p>\n<p><b><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"color:#153d63;background:white;\">Researcher in project PARADOx | </span></b><span style=\"color:#002328;\"><a href=\"http://www.paradoxscience.nl/\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">www.paradoxscience.nl/</a> | L</span><span style=\"color:#002328;\">aatste </span><span style=\"color:#153d63;\"><a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/43d123691084/guq1urhmn5-12703426?e=8fddfee5c1\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" title=\"https://mailchi.mp/43d123691084/guq1urhmn5-12703426?e=8fddfee5c1\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#153d63;\">nieuwsbrief</span></a></span></p>\n<p><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"background:white;\"> </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"color:#201f1e;\">Daily parenting dynamics are adolescent-specific: <i><a href=\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10964-023-01912-5\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" title=\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10964-023-01912-5\" target=\"_blank\">Journal of Youth and Adolescence</a><br>\n</i></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"background:white;\">Working days: Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, &amp; Friday</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"background:white;\"></span></p>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"width:356.25pt;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt;\">\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n</div>",
